WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.160
So one of the things too

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.480
that maybe not everybody knows about

3
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.920
is there are time of day differences

4
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.180
in muscle strength.

5
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.700
So humans are stronger in the afternoon

6
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.850
than they are in the morning.

7
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.260
There's about 25 studies on this,

8
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.560
it's pretty convincing.

9
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.420
The other thing that has been demonstrated out there

10
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.150
is that the mitochondria,

11
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.240
the oxygen consumption rate of mitochondria

12
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.400
in your muscles is higher

13
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.320
in the afternoon, early evening

14
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.300
than it is in the morning.

15
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.720
And so that has significant associations

16
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.600
with performance.

17
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.220
And in fact,

18
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.720
there are other groups that have done,

19
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.320
if you take a regular mouse strain,

20
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.980
and you have them do an endurance running test

21
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.660
in the morning,

22
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.400
and then you test the same ones

23
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.540
different day, whatever, in the afternoon,

24
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.040
they have a lot more endurance in the afternoon

25
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.220
than they do in the morning,

26
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.480
consistent with the idea

27
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.420
that your mitochondria are working better

28
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:52.980
at that time.

29
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.960
So what a postdoc did is he said,

30
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.620
okay, well, what happens if I train them?

31
00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.120
Let's just train them in the morning.

32
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.640
And let's see if that difference

33
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.200
between morning performance and afternoon performance

34
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.320
stays or does it go away?

35
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.000
What happens?

36
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.670
And the simple answer is it goes away.

37
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.290
But it takes weeks, right?
